# Security headers applied to every route
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-XSS-Protection: 1; mode=block
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(self)
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  # Content Security Policy — closes Sam's M2 finding.
  # 'unsafe-inline' on scripts is required for Next.js static export hydration
  # data (__NEXT_DATA__). Follow-up: tighten with nonces or hashes once we
  # move off static export or add a build-time CSP hash injector.
  # frame-src allows Google Maps embed (used on / and /contact).
  # img-src allows any https: source so Dealer Center photo CDN works.
  # connect-src includes dms.loveautogroup.net for the LeadForm submit
  # (POST /api/v1/public/leads) and any client-side inventory/merchandising
  # fetches. Without this, the browser blocks the cross-origin fetch with
  # "Failed to fetch" before the request even leaves — server logs stay empty.
  # 2026-05-05 — script-src + connect-src whitelisted for static.cargurus.com
  # 2026-06-07 — connect-src += vpic.nhtsa.dot.gov (sell-your-car VIN decode, W1)
  # 2026-06-24 — connect-src += www.cargurus.com: the deal-rating badge SDK
  # 2026-06-29 (S2-1): GA4 — script-src += googletagmanager.com; connect-src +=
  #   googletagmanager + google-analytics (+ region/analytics subdomains) so gtag
  #   loads and beacons aren't CSP-blocked (the CarGurus-badge lesson).
  #   (loaded from static.cargurus.com) POSTs the rating request to
  #   www.cargurus.com/Cars/api/1.0/dealRatingRequest.action — without this the
  #   browser CSP-blocked it (confirmed via CarGurus support console paste).
  # so the CarGurus deal-rating badge in layout.tsx can finally execute.
  # Charlotte's audit (marketing-audit-2026-05-05/seo-audit.md) found CSP
  # was silently blocking the badge — it had never rendered. The May-2 503
  # finding was a red herring; the CDN is fine, our policy was the blocker.
  # 2026-06-07 (S27): script-src/connect-src += cloudflareinsights (the W2
  # RUM beacon was CSP-blocked since May 5). A dealercenter frame-src entry
  # added earlier that day was removed again the same day — the hosted
  # iframe was replaced by the in-house credit application (FinancingForm
  # -> dms.loveautogroup.net, already in connect-src).
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cargurus.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com https://www.googletagmanager.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self' data:; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; connect-src 'self' https://dms.loveautogroup.net https://static.cargurus.com https://www.cargurus.com https://vpic.nhtsa.dot.gov https://cloudflareinsights.com https://www.googletagmanager.com https://www.google-analytics.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://o4511298664202240.ingest.us.sentry.io; frame-src https://www.google.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# Admin routes — noindex, no cache. Auth is the __Secure-lag_admin session
# cookie (functions/_lib/admin-auth.ts), NOT Cloudflare Access — no Access
# application has ever been configured for this site.
# NOTE: per Cloudflare docs, _headers rules do NOT apply to responses
# generated by Pages Functions. The rules below cover static assets only;
# /api/admin/* handlers must set these headers themselves.
/admin/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive
  Cache-Control: no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate, private
/api/admin/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive
  Cache-Control: no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate, private

# ── Caching ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `immutable` means "never revalidate, not even on reload". That is a promise
# about the URL, not the file: it is only honest when the FILENAME changes
# whenever the bytes change.
#
# ⚠️ THIS RULE USED TO BE BLANKET, BY EXTENSION, AND IT MADE EVERY ASSET IN
# public/ WRITE-ONCE. 650 files sat at stable paths under a one-year immutable
# promise, so editing one changed nothing that anybody could see. The logo is
# the case that proved it: logo-primary.svg was corrected on 2026-08-11, the
# deploy went green, the origin bytes were right, and the live site kept
# serving the old logo because nothing ever re-requested the file
# (cf-cache-status: HIT, Age ~13 days, and browser copies pinned for a year).
# The fix was a new filename, which is the only thing that works once a URL
# has been declared immutable.
#
# Two different kinds of asset, so two different rules:

# 1. Next.js build output. The filename IS a content hash
#    (chunks/00m0-r~h.hnn..js), so a change always produces a new URL.
#    immutable is both correct and load-bearing here — without it the browser
#    revalidates every chunk on every navigation.
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# 2. Everything else — logos, brand art, vehicle photos, favicons. These live
#    at STABLE, hand-written paths and are edited in place, so they must stay
#    reachable by a new version. Still cached hard at the edge; the browser
#    just re-checks hourly instead of assuming for a year, and a revalidation
#    that finds no change costs a 304, not a re-download.
/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400
/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400
/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400
/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400
/*.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400
/*.jpeg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400
/*.webp
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400
/*.avif
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400
/*.woff
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400
/*.woff2
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400
/*.ico
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400
